# Watchlist and Alerts Room

The Watchlist and Alerts Room is the first Nadi Plus habit layer. It lets an investor save funds for research follow-up, create simple review triggers, and connect the screener, X-Ray, Coach, and Journal into a repeatable process. In this prototype, watchlists and alerts are saved in browser local storage only.

## Alert types

- Review date: reminds the investor to inspect the fund again on a planned date.
- Expense ratio above: flags when a demo expense ratio crosses the user's threshold.
- Drawdown above: flags when demo drawdown is above the planned comfort band.
- Nadi score below: flags when the demo research score falls below a floor.
- Style or manager check: creates a qualitative review marker for future factsheet or AMC communication checks.

## Product posture

The room should feel like disciplined research tracking, not advice. It can say "review this", "attention", "within limit", "watch", or "inspect evidence". It should not say "buy", "sell", "switch", "best for you", or "guaranteed". Once live data is connected, every triggered alert should show the source date and evidence record that created the alert state.

## Monetization use

The Watchlist and Alerts Room is a strong Phase 1 paid feature because it sells organization, saved history, alerts, and discipline rather than fund distribution. Free users can receive a small sample of the workflow; Nadi Plus can unlock unlimited watched funds, alert history, exports, and future email or WhatsApp reminders after consent design.
